From: Tetris Linux bring-up
Subject: [PATCH] mailbox: mediatek: retain GPUEB claims after failed boot attempt

remoteproc start/attach can fail after hardware has begun accessing memory.
An absent successful boot reference is not evidence of physical shutdown.
Keep all claims and references after an attempted boot that returned an error,
even if the remoteproc core restored its logical OFFLINE state. This deliberately
does not invent an OFF acknowledgement or call shutdown without a reference.
Activation still requires an audited physical stop contract in the real owner.

--- a/drivers/pmdomain/mediatek/mt6878-gpueb-session.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/mediatek/mt6878-gpueb-session.c
@@ -40,5 +40,5 @@
 	phys_addr_t shared_pa;
 	u32 magic, reply[GPUEB_WORDS];
-	bool waiting, initialized, boot_ref;
+	bool waiting, initialized, boot_ref, boot_attempted;
 	int error;
 };
@@ -225,4 +225,10 @@
 static bool gpueb_release(struct mt6878_gpueb_session *s)
 {
+	/*
+	 * rproc_boot() errors can follow a partial hardware start. Core state
+	 * alone cannot authorize freeing memory in that case.
+	 */
+	if (s->boot_attempted && !s->boot_ref)
+		return false;
 	if (s->boot_ref) {
 		if (rproc_shutdown(s->rproc) ||
@@ -361,4 +367,5 @@
 		goto fail;
 	}
+	s->boot_attempted = true;
 	ret = rproc_boot(s->rproc);
 	if (ret)
